===Verb===
{{en-verb|++}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take a photograph of.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1904|author=David T Hanbury|title=Sport and Travel in the Northland of Canada|passage=As he did not appear disposed to move off, I took my camera and approached within about thirty yards, when I '''snapshotted''' him.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To capture the state of, in a snapshot.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=David E. Irwin|title=An Operating System Architecture for Networked Server Infrastructure|page=30
|passage=Filer appliances also offer programmatic '''snapshotting''' and cloning at the block-level or file system-level.}}

